Refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for a description of the "Gst-NvDsUcx"
plugin.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
Hardware:
-Nvidia ConnectX-6 DX or newer

Software:
-Mellanox OFED-5.5-1.0.3.2
-UCX-v1.12.1 (compiled with CUDA support)

The DeepStream SDK documentation has instructions on installing required software.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the plugin:
Export or set in Makefile the appropriate CUDA_VER
Run make and sudo make install

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sender:
gst-launch-1.0 -e videotestsrc ! queue ! nvvideoconvert ! \
'video/x-raw(memory:NVMM),format=NV12,width=480,height=360,framerate=3000/1, gpu-id=1' ! \
nvdsucxserversink addr=$ADDR port=$PORT

Reciver:
gst-launch-1.0 -e nvdsucxclientsrc addr=$ADDR port=$PORT nvbuf-memory-type=2 num-nvbuf=4 ! \
'video/x-raw(memory:NVMM),format=NV12,width=480,height=360,framerate=3000/1' ! \
queue ! nvvideoconvert ! \
fpsdisplaysink video-sink=fakesink text-overlay=false signal-fps-measurements=true sync=0
